        Summary: For any integer \(k\), we prove the existence of a uniquely \(k\)-colourable graph of girth at least \(g\) on at most \(k^{12(g+1)}\) vertices whose maximal degree is at most \(5k^{13}\). From this we deduce that, unless NP=RP, no polynomial time algorithm for \(k\)-colourability on graphs \(G\) of girth \(g(G)\geq{\log| G|\over 13\log k}\) and maximum degree \(\Delta(G)\leq 6k^{13}\) can exist. We also study several related problems.
