        Summary: It is shown that the clique polynomial is a parent polynomial of the chromatic polynomial, adjoint polynomial and the \(\sigma\)-polynomial. Colouring concepts such as chromatic number, chromatic equivalence and unique colourability are described in terms of clique covers. Some general theorems, resulting from the interconnections, are deduced. Finally, general constructions are given for infinite families of uniquely colourable graphs.
