        Summary: Given a digraph $D$ with no loops, the \textit{dicoloring graph} of $D$, denoted by $\mathcal{D}_k(D)$, is the graph whose vertices are the acyclic $k$-colorings of $D$ and two colorings are adjacent in $\mathcal{D}_k(D)$ if they differ in color on exactly one vertex. In this paper, we prove that there is no expression $ϕ(\vecχ)$ in terms of the dichromatic number $\vecχ$, such that the graph $\mathcal{D}_k(D)$ is connected for all graphs $D$ and integers $k\geq ϕ(\vecχ)$. We give conditions for the dicoloring graph of two infinite families of circulant tournaments to be connected, an
